Subject: [PATCH 29/41] =?UTF-8?q?hottyterm:=20edit=20commands=20and=20prog?=
 =?UTF-8?q?rams'=20menus=20(SPEC=20=C2=A710.5,=20=C2=A710.6)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mod is Command on macOS and Control elsewhere. A key of an edit command
the program took (a=edit, per screen, dropped on leaving the alternate
screen and on RIS) reaches it as the event command: a copy with a
selection on the cells copies it instead, and a paste reads the
clipboard first. A program's which-key menu (a=menu), from the cells or
a surface, shows at the bottom right of the screen, and a key it does
not list hides it. Key sequences are the program's (HOTTY 0.3): a key
its keymap binds to prefix hands it the keys after it.

Upstream files: Surface.zig +1 (the paste command's hook).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
